WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.550
Augustine of Hippo, who
died in 430, faced a puzzle.

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.370
Christians were taught
to love their enemies.

3
00:00:07.420 --> 00:00:09.860
Yet some of them served as soldiers.

4
00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:14.280
Centuries later, Thomas Aquinas
tried to answer the same puzzle.

5
00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:17.220
So can a war ever be fought justly?

6
00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:19.270
And who decides the rules?

7
00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.770
In this mission, you'll see how
Christians have tried to answer it,

8
00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:24.820
from Augustine to today.

9
00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:30.320
Then you'll weigh up a hard claim:
is a just war still possible today?

10
00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:33.910
Your mission: find out when
a war could count as just,

11
00:00:33.960 --> 00:00:35.470
and who sets the rules.
